Saphira OpenStack storage role (cinder LVM host)
==================================================

Install this package on the machine that will hold volumes, then run,
as root:

    saphira-openstack-setup-storage

It asks which controller to serve, the credentials, and which DISK to
devote to volumes — then creates the volume group, registers the
cinder identity and endpoints, and writes cinder.conf.

Read this before you run it: the iSCSI target daemon (tgt /
open-iscsi) is NOT a Saphira package yet, so no host can export
volumes today. The script prepares everything up to that gate and
stops there honestly instead of pretending. When the target packages
land, re-run the script and it picks up exactly where it stopped.

Disk safety (enforced by the script, obey it anyway):
  - Point it at an EMPTY disk. It refuses mounted filesystems and
    existing partition tables unless you type YES.
  - Snapshot or back up anything you value BEFORE pvcreate.
    pvcreate on the wrong disk eats a partition table in one second.

Verify later with:

    saphira-openstack-setup-storage --check

Full story (how-to, pitfalls, do and don't):
saphira-openstack-documentation.
Saphira Linux — "It's so Simple it Hurts."
